    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d486">

                <pb facs="0457" n="341" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg341"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/481.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Dominican Republic to the Secretary of
                            State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-01-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 19, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Minister for Foreign Affairs requests me to inform you that the Haitian
                    authorities of Cape Haitien have sent Desiderio Arias<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d486-f1"/> by sea 200 rifles and 10,000 rounds of ammunition, and
                    that a Dominican revolutionist left Cape Haitien with the arms and
                    ammunition.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d486-f1" n="1" xml:id="d486-f1-content">
                <p>One of the insurrectionary leaders; see <ref target="frus1911#pg_173">For. Rel.
                        1911, p. 173</ref>. The other principals were Horacio Vásquez and Luis
                    Felipe Vidal.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
